{"command": "cd /testbed && cat > /tmp/const.txt <<'EOF'\n# tinydb Constitution\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### I. Preserve Existing Public API Behavior\nNew features MUST wrap or extend existing components without changing the\nobservable behavior of existing public APIs. Existing callers of the ordinary\n`TinyDB` interfaces MUST continue to work unchanged. Any new entry point\n(e.g. `tinydb.journal.BatchWriter`) MUST be additive and MUST NOT alter the\nsemantics of preexisting methods.\nRationale: this milestone adds a journal/batch layer on top of TinyDB; breaking\nthe ordinary read/write contract would invalidate every downstream consumer.\n\n### II. Testable Acceptance Criteria\nEvery requirement MUST carry at least one objective, observable acceptance\ncriterion that a test can check (concrete input to expected output or\nexception). Vague language (\"should\", \"fast\", \"easy\") is NOT acceptable in a\nrequirement; state the concrete behavior and its observable result.\nRationale: requirements such as R01-R03 must be verifiable by `pytest`\n(see `acceptance_public.py`) without interpretation.\n\n### III. Evidence Over Assertion\nClaims about behavior MUST be backed by observed evidence (a run command and\nits output, or a passing test). Distinguish explicitly between what was\nobserved and what is assumed or unverified. Do NOT report a test as run\nwithout a command and its output as evidence.\nRationale: autonomous work has no human to confirm results; only reproducible\nevidence is trustworthy.\n\n### IV. Simple, Scoped Implementations\nPrefer the smallest implementation that satisfies the stated requirements.\nDo NOT add speculative features, abstractions, or configuration beyond the\nscope of the current requirement (YAGNI). Keep changes local to the affected\nmodule (e.g. `tinydb/journal.py`).\nRationale: scope creep and unrequested generality increase risk and review\ncost without adding required value.\n\n### V. Document Assumptions and Regressions\nUnresolved assumptions, open questions, and any regressions introduced MUST be\nrecorded in writing (e.g. `HANDOFF.md` and the relevant spec/plan documents)\nrather than left implicit. A regression MUST be named, its trigger described,\nand its status (open/fixed) stated.\nRationale: later phases and reviewers need an explicit record of what is\nsettled versus what is still open.\n\n## Additional Constraints\n\n- Implementation source for the batch feature is `tinydb/journal.py`.\n- The batch writer MUST target the default table only.\n- Upstream tests MUST remain unchanged; do not modify `acceptance_public.py`.\n- Public acceptance is defined by `acceptance_public.py`.\n\n## Development Workflow\n\n- Work proceeds through the Spec Kit phases (constitution, specify, clarify,\n  plan, tasks, implement, converge) in order.\n- Application implementation is deferred to later phases; this phase only\n  establishes governance.\n- Keep documents concise and make evidence explicit.\n- Feature artifacts live under `specs/001-transactions`.\n\n## Governance\n\nThis constitution supersedes all other conflicting practices in the project.\nAmendments require a written change to this file, a semantic version bump\n(MAJOR for removed/redefined principles, MINOR for added principles or\nmaterially expanded guidance, PATCH for clarifications), and an updated\n`Last Amended` date. Compliance is reviewed at each phase boundary; a phase\nMUST NOT be declared done while a principle is violated.\n\n**Version**: 1.0.0 | **Ratified**: 2026-10-17 | **Last Amended**: 2026-10-17\nEOF\ncp /tmp/const.txt .specify/memory/constitution.md && echo WROTE && head -5 .specify/memory/constitution.md && grep -c 'Version' .specify/memory/constitution.md", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": "WROTE\n# tinydb Constitution\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### I. Preserve Existing Public API Behavior\n1\n"}